hen $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[30,110],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{30+110}{2}=70\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean time to fix the leaky pipe is $70\\,\\text{min}.$"] ["question-34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b"] ["answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d" :answer/id #uuid "04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d"] ["answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d" :answer/value "110\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735" :answer/id #uuid "8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735"] ["answer-8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735" :answer/value "140\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c" :answer/id #uuid "91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c"] ["answer-91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c" :answer/value "30\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4" :answer/id #uuid "df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4"] ["answer-df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4" :answer/value "37\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6" :answer/id #uuid "c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6"] ["answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6" :answer/value "70\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/correct "answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4"] ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/choices "answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6"] ["question-34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b"] [17592186157376 :knowledge-point/questions "question-34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/id #uuid "ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96961"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/problem "The duration of a tv program is uniformly distributed between $24$ and $36$ minutes, inclusive. What is the variance of the TV program duration?"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the duration of a tv program. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[24,36],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[24,36],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(36-24)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{144}{12}=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the TV program duration is $12\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}.$"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc"] ["answer-a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869" :answer/id #uuid "a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869"] ["answer-a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869" :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}"] ["answer-c84d385d-e171-5620-9eeb-5a8f85a098a7" :answer/id #uuid "c84d385d-e171-5620-9eeb-5a8f85a098a7"] ["answer-c84d385d-e171-5620-9eeb-5a8f85a098a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c84d385d-e171-5620-9eeb-5a8f85a098a7" :answer/value "14\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}"] ["answer-0b4b9d86-b8c2-53ab-aeb4-85c153141813" :answer/id #uuid "0b4b9d86-b8c2-53ab-aeb4-85c153141813"] ["answer-0b4b9d86-b8c2-53ab-aeb4-85c153141813" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b4b9d86-b8c2-53ab-aeb4-85c153141813" :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}"] ["answer-8879f320-bcc2-587d-aaca-28c7f3bdd676" :answer/id #uuid "8879f320-bcc2-587d-aaca-28c7f3bdd676"] ["answer-8879f320-bcc2-587d-aaca-28c7f3bdd676" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8879f320-bcc2-587d-aaca-28c7f3bdd676" :answer/value "26\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}"] ["answer-93677d4d-73a3-5753-b99e-accf2ba9f954" :answer/id #uuid "93677d4d-73a3-5753-b99e-accf2ba9f954"] ["answer-93677d4d-73a3-5753-b99e-accf2ba9f954" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-93677d4d-73a3-5753-b99e-accf2ba9f954" :answer/value "36\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/correct "answer-a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/choices "answer-a26a89f6-b7c9-5842-8fd9-8cb26c1f5869"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/choices "answer-c84d385d-e171-5620-9eeb-5a8f85a098a7"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b4b9d86-b8c2-53ab-aeb4-85c153141813"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/choices "answer-8879f320-bcc2-587d-aaca-28c7f3bdd676"] ["answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc" :answer-field/choices "answer-93677d4d-73a3-5753-b99e-accf2ba9f954"] ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-fa393c5b-69a5-51b3-a77d-1f39127b18dc"] [17592186157377 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/id #uuid "881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96956"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/problem "The distance covered per game by a football player in an official match is uniformly distributed between $9$ km and $12$ km, inclusive. What is the variance in the distance covered by this player?"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by the player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[9,12],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[9,12],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(12-9)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{9}{12}=\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the distance covered by the football player is $\\frac{3}{4}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}.$"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7"] ["answer-e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c" :answer/id #uuid "e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c"] ["answer-e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}"] ["answer-50116483-a706-5dd6-a017-943ddc486998" :answer/id #uuid "50116483-a706-5dd6-a017-943ddc486998"] ["answer-50116483-a706-5dd6-a017-943ddc486998" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-50116483-a706-5dd6-a017-943ddc486998" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}"] ["answer-c6ceb90f-a5c7-55b2-90f2-a1d30c0c01a6" :answer/id #uuid "c6ceb90f-a5c7-55b2-90f2-a1d30c0c01a6"] ["answer-c6ceb90f-a5c7-55b2-90f2-a1d30c0c01a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c6ceb90f-a5c7-55b2-90f2-a1d30c0c01a6" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}"] ["answer-daa1ca2a-c1b0-5926-8a0e-e922c3c89348" :answer/id #uuid "daa1ca2a-c1b0-5926-8a0e-e922c3c89348"] ["answer-daa1ca2a-c1b0-5926-8a0e-e922c3c89348" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-daa1ca2a-c1b0-5926-8a0e-e922c3c89348" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}"] ["answer-7f0cd53c-7363-5ab5-92fc-590bf229d977" :answer/id #uuid "7f0cd53c-7363-5ab5-92fc-590bf229d977"] ["answer-7f0cd53c-7363-5ab5-92fc-590bf229d977" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7f0cd53c-7363-5ab5-92fc-590bf229d977" :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/correct "answer-e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-e063d08e-9e0a-5ed0-ab66-0020ccdffa4c"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-50116483-a706-5dd6-a017-943ddc486998"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-c6ceb90f-a5c7-55b2-90f2-a1d30c0c01a6"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-daa1ca2a-c1b0-5926-8a0e-e922c3c89348"] ["answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-7f0cd53c-7363-5ab5-92fc-590bf229d977"] ["question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9740dd9c-a42e-5b17-8af5-62f3038a4eb7"] [17592186157377 :knowledge-point/questions "question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3"] [17592186158009 :question/problem "The time it takes a mechanic to repair a car is uniformly distributed with a minimum of $2$ hours and a maximum of $6$ hours. What is the variance of the time it takes to repair a car?"] [17592186158009 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the time it takes to repair a car. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[2,6],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[2,6],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(6-2)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the time it takes to repair a car is $\\frac{4}{3}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}$"] [17592186158009 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-5198a366-384f-526c-a099-9dad65d5986e" :answer/id #uuid "5198a366-384f-526c-a099-9dad65d5986e"] ["answer-5198a366-384f-526c-a099-9dad65d5986e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5198a366-384f-526c-a099-9dad65d5986e" :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-05252ab4-17c7-54ff-8a99-a05918ce2b8f" :answer/id #uuid "05252ab4-17c7-54ff-8a99-a05918ce2b8f"] ["answer-05252ab4-17c7-54ff-8a99-a05918ce2b8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-05252ab4-17c7-54ff-8a99-a05918ce2b8f" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-dd9f857e-b1eb-5a2b-a336-0e4b6cc339b3" :answer/id #uuid "dd9f857e-b1eb-5a2b-a336-0e4b6cc339b3"] ["answer-dd9f857e-b1eb-5a2b-a336-0e4b6cc339b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dd9f857e-b1eb-5a2b-a336-0e4b6cc339b3" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-9992cae0-ada8-57b8-84ad-c508b7212276" :answer/id #uuid "9992cae0-ada8-57b8-84ad-c508b7212276"] ["answer-9992cae0-ada8-57b8-84ad-c508b7212276" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9992cae0-ada8-57b8-84ad-c508b7212276" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{13}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d" :answer/id #uuid "1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d"] ["answer-1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/correct "answer-1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices "answer-5198a366-384f-526c-a099-9dad65d5986e"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices "answer-05252ab4-17c7-54ff-8a99-a05918ce2b8f"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices "answer-dd9f857e-b1eb-5a2b-a336-0e4b6cc339b3"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices "answer-9992cae0-ada8-57b8-84ad-c508b7212276"] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices "answer-1971a4b2-550b-5394-b1b5-b2ce91a4486d"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/id #uuid "b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96950"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/problem "A librarian has noticed that the minimum visiting time of a visitor is $0.5$ hours, whereas the maximum time is $6.5$ hours. If the visiting time is uniformly distributed, what is its variance?"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the visiting time of a randomly chosen visitor. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[0.5,6.5],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[0.5,6.5],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(6.5-0.5)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{36}{12}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance  is $3\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}.$"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441"] ["answer-e9766f35-9561-5089-93e8-b3efe0163bc9" :answer/id #uuid "e9766f35-9561-5089-93e8-b3efe0163bc9"] ["answer-e9766f35-9561-5089-93e8-b3efe0163bc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e9766f35-9561-5089-93e8-b3efe0163bc9" :answer/value "3.5\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-e058e338-722a-56b0-801a-88babf877d02" :answer/id #uuid "e058e338-722a-56b0-801a-88babf877d02"] ["answer-e058e338-722a-56b0-801a-88babf877d02" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e058e338-722a-56b0-801a-88babf877d02" :answer/value "3.6\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d" :answer/id #uuid "37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d"] ["answer-37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d" :answer/value "3\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-3ec20181-951b-5f69-b8f4-a198ce2328f2" :answer/id #uuid "3ec20181-951b-5f69-b8f4-a198ce2328f2"] ["answer-3ec20181-951b-5f69-b8f4-a198ce2328f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3ec20181-951b-5f69-b8f4-a198ce2328f2" :answer/value "6.5\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-f372aa5a-6bd3-5dfe-a21b-5891bbe6d4d0" :answer/id #uuid "f372aa5a-6bd3-5dfe-a21b-5891bbe6d4d0"] ["answer-f372aa5a-6bd3-5dfe-a21b-5891bbe6d4d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f372aa5a-6bd3-5dfe-a21b-5891bbe6d4d0" :answer/value "6\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/correct "answer-37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9766f35-9561-5089-93e8-b3efe0163bc9"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/choices "answer-e058e338-722a-56b0-801a-88babf877d02"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/choices "answer-37c899a0-311c-5b6b-9ff3-e7d42dfa323d"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/choices "answer-3ec20181-951b-5f69-b8f4-a198ce2328f2"] ["answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441" :answer-field/choices "answer-f372aa5a-6bd3-5dfe-a21b-5891bbe6d4d0"] ["question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a4dcef72-956c-59fb-8c70-71f6c1dcf441"] [17592186157377 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/id #uuid "fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/math-academy-id "q-96953"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/problem "A video game randomly generates an obstacle the player has to avoid. The obstacle's $x$-coordinate is uniformly distributed along a segment whose endpoints have $x$-coordinates of $16$ and $24.$ What is the variance of the $x$-coordinate of the obstacle?"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the randomly generated $x$-coordinate of the obstacle. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[16,24],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[16,24],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(24-16)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{64}{12}=\\frac{16}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the $x$-coordinate is $\\frac{16}{3}.$"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/id #uuid "101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10"] ["answer-7f654726-55d0-5fca-9cdd-7a52ab9a67b2" :answer/id #uuid "7f654726-55d0-5fca-9cdd-7a52ab9a67b2"] ["answer-7f654726-55d0-5fca-9cdd-7a52ab9a67b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7f654726-55d0-5fca-9cdd-7a52ab9a67b2" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e" :answer/id #uuid "c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e"] ["answer-c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e" :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["answer-06fa8f9c-5850-57e0-979a-29fbc9973afa" :answer/id #uuid "06fa8f9c-5850-57e0-979a-29fbc9973afa"] ["answer-06fa8f9c-5850-57e0-979a-29fbc9973afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-06fa8f9c-5850-57e0-979a-29fbc9973afa" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{13}"] ["answer-600f499f-c1d3-5ae0-b4a1-160b380ead3c" :answer/id #uuid "600f499f-c1d3-5ae0-b4a1-160b380ead3c"] ["answer-600f499f-c1d3-5ae0-b4a1-160b380ead3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-600f499f-c1d3-5ae0-b4a1-160b380ead3c" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}"] ["answer-60225bce-dd95-55d2-bd3a-e4a05b09a0ed" :answer/id #uuid "60225bce-dd95-55d2-bd3a-e4a05b09a0ed"] ["answer-60225bce-dd95-55d2-bd3a-e4a05b09a0ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-60225bce-dd95-55d2-bd3a-e4a05b09a0ed" :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/correct "answer-c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/choices "answer-7f654726-55d0-5fca-9cdd-7a52ab9a67b2"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/choices "answer-c3be71c0-f54f-59b2-826c-729857d8c48e"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/choices "answer-06fa8f9c-5850-57e0-979a-29fbc9973afa"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/choices "answer-600f499f-c1d3-5ae0-b4a1-160b380ead3c"] ["answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10" :answer-field/choices "answer-60225bce-dd95-55d2-bd3a-e4a05b09a0ed"] ["question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-101a0955-c20d-5d60-8f35-d4ac4d90df10"] [17592186157377 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581"] [17592186158542 :tutorial/content "In general, if $X \\sim U[a,b]$ is uniformly distributed, then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/93/93894f939fa0ef715ee6ab6c225f456972b746184673df0b8d8312656727d793.svg)\n\nWe can use a continuous uniform distribution to model situations where all possible outcomes on a finite interval are equally likely.\n\nFor instance, suppose a dental receptionist wants to model the waiting time of a randomly selected patient. After observing a number of patients over several days, the receptionist notices that the waiting time is uniformly distributed between $6$ and $14$ minutes, inclusive.\n\nThen, by letting $X$ be the amount of time a randomly selected patient spends waiting, we can model the waiting time using the continuous uniform distribution: \n\n$$\nX \\sim U[6,14]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/fd/fd37b3e19aad197ebb7eeabad00fca068455eed8da462a12630134cd7980941e.svg)\n\nWith this model, we can now make predictions about patient waiting times.\n\nFor example, the probability that a randomly selected patient waits longer than $9$ minutes is equal to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 9) & ={\\int }_{9}^{14}\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{9}^{14}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[x]}_{9}^{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[14-9] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can also calculate the mean waiting time by finding the expected value of $X\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =\\frac{a+b}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+14}{2} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean waiting time is $10$ minutes."] [17592186157536 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0]] "retractions" [[17592186157195 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the duration of the radio program. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[27,34]$, and we wish to compute $P(X < 30)$.\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b]$, then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{b - a},\\begin{vmatrix}a \\le x \\le b \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[27,34]$, we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{7},\\begin{vmatrix}27 \\le x \\le 34 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X < 30) &= \\int_{27}^{30}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{27}^{30}\\frac{1}{7}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x}{7}\\right|_{27}^{30} \\\\\n&= \\frac{30}{7} - \\frac{27}{7} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186157196 :question/problem "A video game randomly generates an obstacle the player has to avoid. The obstacle's $x$-coordinate is uniformly distributed along a segment whose endpoints have $x$-coordinates of $-6$ and $12$. What is the mean $x$-coordinate of the obstacle?"] [17592186157196 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the $x$-coordinate of a randomly generated obstacle. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[-6,12]$, and we wish to compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b]$, then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[-6,12]$, we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{-6+12}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean $x$-coordinate is $3$."] [17592186157197 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the visiting time of a randomly chosen visitor. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[1.5,4.5]$, and we wish to compute $\\textrm{Var}[X]$.\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b]$, then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(b-a)^2}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[1.5,4.5]$, we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(4.5-1.5)^2}{12} = \\dfrac{9}{12} = \\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{hr}^2\n$$"] [17592186158009 :question/problem "The time it takes a mechanic to repair a car is uniformly distributed with a minimum of $2$ hours and a maximum of $6$ hours. What is the variance of the time it takes to repair a car?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156976] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156977] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156978] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156979] [17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156980] [17592186158542 :tutorial/content "In general, if $X \\sim U[a,b]$ is uniformly distributed, then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{b - a},\\begin{vmatrix}a \\le x \\le b \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nWe can use a continuous uniform distribution to model situations where all possible outcomes on a finite interval are equally likely.\n\nFor instance, suppose a dental receptionist wants to model the waiting time of a randomly selected patient. After observing a number of patients over several days, the receptionist notices that the waiting time is uniformly distributed between $6$ and $14$ minutes, inclusive.\n\nThen, by letting $X$ be the amount of time a randomly selected patient spends waiting, we can model the waiting time using the continuous uniform distribution:\n\n$$\nX \\sim U[6,14]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{8},\\begin{vmatrix}6 \\le x \\le 14 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nWith this model, we can now make predictions about patient waiting times.\n\nFor example, the probability that a randomly selected patient waits longer than $9$ minutes is equal to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\ge 9) &= \\int_{9}^{14}\\frac{1}{8}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\\int_{9}^{14}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[x]_{9}^{14} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[14 - 9] \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can also calculate the mean waiting time by finding the expected value of $X$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\frac{a + b}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{6 + 14}{2} \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean waiting time is $10$ minutes."]]}]